<title>USA: American Stores may issue $300 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>American Stores may issue $300 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Stores Co is expected to tap the corporate bond primary market with a $300 million two-part debt offering next week, syndicate sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Baa2/BBB-plus rated deal is expected to include $100 million in 20-year noncallable debt and $200 million in 40-year debt which is putable in 12 years, sources said.</p>
<p>The offering is expected to be underwritten by lead manager JP Morgan Securities Inc, they said.</p>
<p>(( -- Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
